  "kind": "bit-matching-detail",
  "title": "FORECAST and FORECAST.LINEAR use plain binary64 sample-mean OLS (not TREND's QR pipeline) and coerce scalar pairs",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 builds 20131 and 20527, FORECAST(x, known_ys, known_xs) and FORECAST.LINEAR(x, known_ys, known_xs) validate singleton blank/error arguments in formula order, return #N/A on shape mismatch, coerce direct scalar known_ys/known_xs while skipping non-numeric elements in ranges/arrays, and compute a + b*x using plain binary64 sample means and centered sums (unlike TREND, which routes through LINEST's stored-PC64 Householder QR pipeline and gives different low bits), returning #DIV/0! when n == 0 or sum((x - mean_x)^2) == 0. Matches 2,984/2,984 full-bank and 70/70 pinned FORECAST rows, and 2,910/2,910 full-bank FORECAST.LINEAR rows.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured across Excel 16.0 build 20131 (70/70 pinned FORECAST rows in witnesses/FORECAST.json) and Excel 16.0.20527 (2,984 FORECAST and 2,910 FORECAST.LINEAR full-bank rows, prefix_metadata rows 89-90, and fn4_questions ql136-145).",
